WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.080
SPEAKER: Welcome to this
episode of "Click to Deploy,"

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.210
a series where we
show you how easy it

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.810
is to deploy a solution from
the Google Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.850
In this episode,
we'll showcase how

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.730
to set up an Elasticsearch
and data flow integration

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.620
via the Cloud Marketplace.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.200
Elastic Cloud now has
native integration

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.210
with Google Cloud
Dataflow, which

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.870
provides customers with
easy and fast data ingestion

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.580
into Elastic Cloud.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.060
Now data from BigQuery, Pub/Sub,
and Google Cloud Storage

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.870
can be directly adjusted to
Elastic via Google Dataflow.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:37.740
Let's start by searching for
Elastic in the marketplace.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.840
We'll choose the solution
labeled Elastic Cloud.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.810
On the Solution page,
make sure to read

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:54.820
through the overview, pricing,
and support to learn more

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.440
about the solution.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:59.740
Pricing for the solution is
billed monthly or annually,

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.180
based on your subscription plan.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.980
You'll notice the
pricing calculator,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.380
which will allow you to model
your estimated monthly cost.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.320
Start by selecting a plan.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.880
We'll keep the default plan.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.460
Next, choose the
correct billing account.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:19.520
Then, make sure to review
the terms of the contract.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.370
If you approve of them, agree
to the additional terms,

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:24.290
which are about
billing and complying

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:27.470
with the license agreement.

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:32.132
Finally, click the Subscribe
button to launch the solution.

00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:34.340
Now let's move on to the
next step, which is managing

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.080
your subscription with Elastic.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.330
You'll need to register
with an Elastic account

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.100
to manage the solution.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.070
Sign up or log in to
your Elastic account.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.940
On Elastic Cloud, you can
create your own deployment.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.550
A deployment includes
Elasticsearch, Kibana,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.620
and other Elastic
Stack features,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.040
allowing you to store,
search, and analyze your data.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:02.110
We'll name our
deployment Test Deploy

00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:04.030
and click the Create
Deployment button

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.610
to launch the deployment.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.360
Make sure to save your
deployment credentials.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.640
And when your deployment
is ready, click Continue.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.440
For the purposes
of this tutorial,

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.880
we'll work to ingest data from
BigQuery to Elasticsearch.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.590
But please note
that you can also

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:26.910
ingest data from Google
Cloud Storage and Pub/Sub.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.400
We'll go back to Google
Cloud Marketplace and type

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.435
in Stack Overflow.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.530
We'll start by ingesting the
popular Stack Overflow data

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.080
set.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.780
We'll use a table called
Stack Overflow posts

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:46.250
under the BigQuery data
set, Stack Overflow.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.680
It has several structured
fields as columns,

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.860
like post body, title,
comment count, et cetera,

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.930
which we'll bring
into Elasticsearch

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.220
to perform free text
search and aggregation.

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.910
Next step is to create a
Dataflow job from a template.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.540
Visit Dataflow and
then go to Jobs.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.835
Choose Create A Job
from the template.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:17.340
Choose name, stackoverflowload1,
and keep the default endpoint.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:23.290
Choose the Dataflow template,
BigQuery to Elasticsearch.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.330
The BigQuery to
Elasticsearch template

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:28.360
is one of Google's
provided templates.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.070
Now fill in the
required parameters,

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:35.935
including your Cloud ID
and base64-encoded API key.

00:03:35.935 --> 00:03:39.400
[ELECTRONIC MUSIC]

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.180
For the Elasticsearch
index field,

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.480
pick an index name where
your data will be loaded.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.960
We'll use the Stack Posts index.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.990
Choose the table and
BigQuery to read from.

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.920
We'll use BigQuery Public
Data Stack Overflow Stack

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.350
Overflow posts.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:13.320
Finally, set your
max workers to 1.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.900
Click Run Jobs to start
the batch processing.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.380
[ELECTRONIC MUSIC]

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.420
When you visit Kibana,
within a few minutes,

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.810
you can see the data flowing
into your Elasticsearch index.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:53.060
And there you have
it, BigQuery data

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:57.920
ingested into Elasticsearch
with the click of a button.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:00.400
If you enjoyed this video,
please subscribe and hit

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.760
the Like button below.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.390
We encourage you to check
out the GCP Marketplace

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.500
and deploy the
solution on your own.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:07.510
Thanks for watching.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:10.560
[ELECTRONIC MUSIC]

